  "passage": "In geography class, students learned about seed vaults, places where seeds are stored for the future. The idea surprised them. They had heard of banks for money, but not for seeds.\nTheir teacher explained that seeds can protect food diversity. If a plant disease, war, or climate problem destroys crops in one area, stored seeds may help people grow them again.\nThe class then created a small \"seed memory box.\" Each student brought seeds from a fruit or vegetable their family often ate and wrote a note about it.\nThe box was not a real vault, but it made the idea personal. Saving seeds was also saving choices for tomorrow's meals.",
